          "culture": "The Diavola is the go-to pizza for those who prefer bold, punchy flavors. It is a staple of Italian pizzerias and a symbol of southern Italian boldness in cooking — the south's love of heat expressed in pizza form. Its name and reputation make it the pizza of choice for adventurous diners.",
          "variations": "A version called Pizza Inferno doubles the heat with fresh chili peppers added before and after baking. Some pizzerias pair the salami with nduja, the spreadable spicy salami from Vibo Valentia, for an even more intense heat."
