      {
        "id": 2202,
        "name": "Bombas (Barcelona Style)",
        "cuisine": "Spanish",
        "origin": "Barceloneta, Barcelona, Spain",
        "year": "Late 19th Century",
        "type": "Non-Veg",
        "description": "Bombas are one of Barcelona's most beloved, historically significant, and deliciously unique tapas, originating in the Barceloneta beach neighborhood — the triangular peninsula of narrow streets and seafood restaurants that extends into the Mediterranean — in the late 19th century and named, according to local legend, after the anarchist bombs that were thrown in the city during the turbulent and violent political era of the time, their round shape being the visual inspiration for the name. Unlike conventional Patatas Bravas, which are simply fried potato chunks, Bombas are spherical croquettes constructed from a specific preparation: freshly boiled potatoes are mashed until smooth and seasoned, then wrapped around a filling of sautéed and spiced ground meat — typically a mixture of seasoned ground pork and beef, or a picadillo of minced meat cooked with garlic, spices, and sometimes a sofrito of tomato — shaped into golf ball-sized spheres by hand, coated in fine breadcrumbs, and deep-fried in olive oil until completely golden and crispy on the outside. The exterior crunch of the breadcrumb coating gives way to a layer of creamy, fluffy mashed potato, and at the center a savory, well-seasoned meat filling that provides a surprising and satisfying contrast. They are served hot from the fryer with both bravas sauce and aioli served generously alongside for dipping. The original Barceloneta establishment La Cova Fumada is widely credited as the inventor of Bombas, and the bar still serves them today using the original recipe in a space that has remained essentially unchanged for over a century. Eating Bombas at a plastic table outside a beachside bar in Barceloneta, accompanied by a cold beer and the sound of the Mediterranean, is considered one of Barcelona's quintessential local food experiences.",
        "images": [
          "spanish/bombas1.jpeg",
          "spanish/bombas2.jpeg",
          "spanish/bombas3.jpeg",
          "spanish/bombas4.jpeg",
          "spanish/bombas5.jpeg"
        ]
      }
