        "origin": "Spain",
        "year": "Late 19th Century",
        "type": "Non-Veg",
        "description": "Croquetas de Bacalao — Salt Cod Croquettes — are the equally celebrated and beloved fish-based sibling of the classic Jamón croqueta, made with desalted salt cod (bacalao) shredded into the béchamel filling and perfumed with garlic and parsley to create a croquette that carries within it centuries of Spanish maritime and gastronomic history. Salt cod — cod fish preserved through salting and drying — was one of the most important foods in the Spanish diet from the medieval period through the modern era, its combination of protein density, long shelf life without refrigeration, and affordability making it an essential staple for the poor and a prestigious Lenten food for the religious. The bacalao used in croquetas must be properly desalted before use: the dried salt cod is submerged in cold water and soaked for 24 to 72 hours, with the water changed every eight hours, to remove the salt and rehydrate the fish to a texture similar to fresh cod while retaining the distinctive concentrated, oceanic flavor that distinguishes it from fresh fish. The desalted bacalao is poached gently in milk or water, then flaked carefully to remove any bones and skin, and shredded into fine pieces. The béchamel is made with the poaching milk to capture all the flavor released by the fish during cooking, then enriched with the shredded bacalao, minced garlic cooked briefly in butter, and flat-leaf parsley. The result is a filling with a gentler, sweeter, more oceanic flavor profile than the saltier, more aggressive jamón version — the bacalao croqueta is considered more elegant and subtle by its devotees, while jamón croqueta enthusiasts consider it the more emotionally satisfying preparation. Both versions are equally revered in the canon of Spanish tapas.",
        "images": [
          "spanish/croquetas-de-bacalao1.jpeg",
          "spanish/croquetas-de-bacalao2.jpeg",
          "spanish/croquetas-de-bacalao3.jpeg",
          "spanish/croquetas-de-bacalao4.jpeg",
          "spanish/croquetas-de-bacalao5.jpeg"
        ]
