          "culture": "Chiles Rellenos de Picadillo are the festive, celebratory version — served at birthday lunches, baptisms, and special family gatherings where the additional time and complexity of the picadillo filling signals the importance of the occasion. They represent the most direct connection between modern Chiles Rellenos and the baroque culinary tradition of colonial Puebla's convent cooking.",
          "variations": "Mole Poblano-braised turkey as the filling — a Puebla-specific luxury version. A version using chicken and almonds. A modern version adding huitlacoche (corn fungus, also called corn truffle) to the filling for an earthy, complex flavor."
