          "culture": "Chicken Massaman is the version that has traveled most successfully to Thai restaurants worldwide, its more familiar protein and shorter cooking time making it the practical choice for restaurants and home cooks outside Thailand. Its gentleness and warm aromatic character make it the Thai curry most universally appreciated across different food cultures.",
          "variations": "A version using a whole spatchcocked chicken roasted with Massaman paste before being added to the coconut milk sauce. A version using free-range chicken (gai baan) for a richer, more flavorful result. A version adding dried apricots or raisins alongside the potatoes for a Persian-inspired sweetness."
