          "variations": "Banana leaf-wrapped fish sekuwa (macha poleko — the Tharu traditional style). A version using mustard paste as the sole marinade base (no other spices) for a pure, sharp mustard flavor. A version adding ground sesame seeds to the marinade for a nuttier character."
